\begin{proof}
Let $R$ be a subring of a field $F$ containing the identity $1_F$. Suppose $x,y\in R$ and $xy=0$. Since the multiplication in $R$ is inherited from $F$, this equation also holds in $F$. Because $F$ is a field, it has no zero divisors, so $x=0$ or $y=0$. Thus $R$ has no zero divisors. Since $R$ contains $1_F$, it is a commutative ring with identity and no zero divisors; hence $R$ is an integral domain.
\end{proof}

